##fileformat=VCFv4.2
##INFO=<Number=1,Type=Integer,Description="d",ID=DP>
##contig=<ID=chr1,length=1000000>
##Authority=VCFv4.2.tex (this fixture's declared version) is silent on structured-header attribute ordering, as is VCFv4.3.tex; the only spec text in any version that names an order is non-binding -- VCFv4.4.tex:134-135/VCFv4.5.tex:132-133, "To aid human readability, the order of fields should be ID, Number, Type, Description, then any optional fields. Implementations must not rely on the order of the fields within structured lines and are not required to preserve field ordering." So an ID-last ##INFO declaration is expected to parse cleanly.
##Authority=bcftools 1.23.1 (htslib 1.23.1), measured 2026-08-17: `bcftools view -h` on this exact declaration exits 0, emits no [W::/[E:: line, and echoes it verbatim -- bcftools does not privilege ID's position over any other attribute's. Pinned live by BcftoolsDependencyTest#testInfoAttributeOrderBcftoolsIgnoresIdPosition. vcf_validator 0.10.2 reads this file not valid under BOTH its 4.2 and 4.3 grammars (same "Error: Error in INFO metadata" text), a verdict that IS attributable to ordering here -- the same declaration in ID-first order validates -- but which is disqualified as evidence anyway, since the same tool rejects the specification's own worked ##META example: see VCF_SPEC_AMBIGUITIES.md's "##META attribute order" table, notes [b] and [d].
##Authority=Generalizes the ##META ID-last probe (meta-attribute-order-id-last.vcf) to a non-##META keyed type, per VCF_SPEC_AMBIGUITIES.md's "##META attribute order" entry's 2026-08-14 extension of the decision from ##META alone to every keyed declaration type. A generalization row, not a control row, since it does not come back clean from both tools.
